{
  "slug": "cortex",
  "name": "Cortex",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Cortex — SDLC Automation Engine by Alpha AI. Automates the entire software development lifecycle from idea to deployment. 37 slash commands, 11 specialized AI agents, and 9 auto-invoked skills covering project scaffolding, autonomous building, code review, testing, security scanning, CI/CD generation, and deployment. Supports Python/FastAPI, Node.js/NestJS, and Java/Spring Boot backends with Next.js frontend. Enforces production-grade standards: JWT auth, layered architecture, OWASP security, and performance best practices — all without human intervention.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **27 skills**, **13 agents**, **55 commands**, **7 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (27): `accessibility` (Auto-invoked when writing or modifying ANY user-facing UI — Next.js/React components, forms, modals, navigation, React Native screens), `alpha-architecture` (ALWAYS auto-invoked on ANY code writing task), `code-review` (Auto-invoked when Claude performs code review tasks), `cortex-brainstorming` (MUST USE before creating any new feature, product, service, or component — including any time a user says…), `cortex-debugging` (MUST USE when diagnosing a FAILURE whose cause is unknown — a bug, failing test, exception, error log,…), `cortex-planning` (MUST USE before any multi-step implementation, refactor, migration, or non-trivial code change — anytime the work spans 3+…), `cortex-tdd` (MUST USE before writing implementation code for any feature, bug fix, or behavior change), `cortex-verification` (MUST USE before claiming any work is 'done', 'fixed', 'complete', 'passing', 'shipped', or 'ready' — including before /ship,…), and 19 more\n- **Agents** (13): `ai-integration-specialist` (Specialized agent for adding AI/ML capabilities to existing applications — designs and implements LLM integration, vector search, semantic…), `architect` (Specialized agent for architectural analysis, design decisions, and codebase structure recommendations), `brand-designer` (Specialized agent for brand identity design — SVG logo generation, color systems, typography selection, design tokens, and brand…), `db-optimizer` (Specialized agent for database performance analysis — identifies slow queries, missing indexes, N+1 problems, and provides optimization recommendations), `devops-engineer` (DevOps and infrastructure specialist), `documentation-writer` (Technical documentation specialist), `feature-analyzer` (Specialized agent for analyzing existing codebases — scans project structure, maps features to code, detects architectural patterns and…), `onboarding-mentor` (Interactive onboarding mentor that answers new developer questions about the codebase, explains patterns, and provides guided tours of…), and 5 more\n- **Commands** (55): `accessibility` (Audit frontend for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance: check semantic HTML, ARIA labels, color contrast, keyboard navigation, screen reader…), `ai-upgrade` (Upgrade a specific feature with AI capabilities), `analyze-project` (Scan an existing codebase to map architecture, identify tech stack, and generate project intelligence), `api-docs` (Auto-generate API documentation from codebase), `audit-setup` (Generate security audit logging system with immutable event trail, compliance reporting (GDPR/SOC2), and suspicious activity alerting), `auto-build` (Fully autonomous product builder), `backup-dr` (Configure automated backup schedules, test restore procedures, and generate disaster recovery runbooks), `changelog` (Auto-generate CHANGELOG.md from git history using Conventional Commits), and 47 more\n- **Hooks** (7): `PreToolUse`, `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `PreCompact`, `TeammateIdle`, `TaskCompleted`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `atlassian`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install cortex@claude-community` from `alphaaiservice/cortex`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
